      "hint": "Factor out the coefficient. Two cases: positive (2x-8=6) OR negative (-(2x-8)=6). Solve each.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Factor: |2x−8| = 2|x−4|. So f(x) = 2|x−4| − 6.",
        "a = 2 (vertical stretch ×2), h = 4 (shift right 4), k = −6 (shift down 6).",
        "KEY CONCEPT: |A| = k means A = k  OR  -(A) = k. So: 2x-8=6  AND  -(2x-8)=6.",
        "Case 1: 2x-8=6 → x = 7.  Case 2: multiply both sides by -1 → 2x-8=-6 → x = 1.",
        "W2.b insight: the ± split is the definition of absolute value. Never skip writing both equations."
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Absolute value. Both intercepts.",
      "feedback_wrong_parent": "The | | symbols mean absolute value.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Isolate: |2x-8|=2|x-4|. Then |x-4|=4 → x=8 or x=0."
    },
